{"title":"What should I ask Tom Griffiths?","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/970889021/0/marginalrevolution~What-should-I-ask-Tom-Griffiths.html","date":1790929797000,"content":"<p>Yes I will be doing a Conversation with him.  Looking at <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom_Griffiths_(cognitive_scientist)\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia</a>:</p>\r\n<blockquote><p><b>Thomas L. Griffiths</b> (born <abbr>c.</abbr><span> 1978</span>)<sup></sup> is an Australian academic who is the Henry R. Luce Professor of Information Technology, Consciousness, and Culture at <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princeton_University\">Princeton University</a>. He studies human decision-making and its connection to problem-solving methods in computation. His book with <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brian_Christian\">Brian Christian</a>, <i><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algorithms_to_Live_By:_The_Computer_Science_of_Human_Decisions\">Algorithms to Live By: The Computer Science of Human Decisions</a></i>, was named one of the “Best Books of 2016” by <i><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MIT_Technology_Review\">MIT Technology Review</a></i>…</p>\r\n<p>Griffiths released <i>The Laws of Thought: The Quest for a Mathematical Theory of the Mind</i> in 2026<i>. Siobhan Roberts</i> describes it as “a rigorous and captivating account of how cognition can be modeled via three mathematical frameworks: <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logic\">logic</a>, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_neural_network\">artificial neural networks</a> (“mathematical systems that emulate the operation of the brain”) and <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Probability_theory\">probability theory</a>.”</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://cocosci.princeton.edu/tom/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">his research page</a>, here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Laws-Thought-Quest-Mathematical-Theory/dp/1250358353/ref=sr_1_1?crid=H4XWV4ZGD3V8&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.XDyJOz9yvJk5VYesu6YS_EdOxq1ZescrkH0p2WZthmKU_7_EoREoxrs0-kC5DqvpCmMJlT1_TPeEZtaCymi8Fw.wZKxDeChmL0j3brmax15eGgzsbSSrHyIeCsH0QezdX4&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=tom+griffiths+laws+of+thought&amp;qid=1790818578&amp;sprefix=tom+griffiths%2Caps%2C615&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">his new book on Amazon</a>, I thought the book was excellent.</p>\r\n<p>So what should I ask him?</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/10/what-should-i-ask-tom-griffiths.html\">What should I ask Tom Griffiths?</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/970889021/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/970889021/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/970889021/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/970889021/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/970889021/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/email20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/20/970889021/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/rss20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/10/what-should-i-ask-tom-griffiths.html#comments\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/comments20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/10/what-should-i-ask-tom-griffiths.html/feed\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/commentsrss20.png\" /></a> \r\n<div><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/10/what-should-i-ask-tom-griffiths.html#comments\"><h3>Comments</h3></a><ul><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/10/what-should-i-ask-tom-griffiths.html#comment-161080128\">I'm curious what thoughts he has, if any, on Jeff Hawkins' ...</a> <i>by ndp_jwh</i></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/10/what-should-i-ask-tom-griffiths.html#comment-161080014\">How would you revamp math education in high school? Possibly ...</a> <i>by JOC</i></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/10/what-should-i-ask-tom-griffiths.html#comment-161079983\">In reply to Al.   p(doom)?</a> <i>by Wayfaring Stranger</i></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/10/what-should-i-ask-tom-griffiths.html#comment-161079974\">Is “consciousness” inexplicable (or: does it resist ...</a> <i>by Edward Burke</i></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/10/what-should-i-ask-tom-griffiths.html#comment-161079970\">Some years ago I enjoyed the algorithms book mentioned by ...</a> <i>by Moral Panic</i></li><li><a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/10/what-should-i-ask-tom-griffiths.html#comments\">Plus 6 more...</a></li></ul></div><h3>Related Stories</h3><ul><li><a href=\"https://marginalr